    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Hepburn returns six months after her first visit. She continues propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning with no missed doses and no lightheadedness, wheeze, tiredness, or low mood. The hands remain steadier than in the winter; the head tremor is unchanged and does not trouble her. She uses the voice strategies on stage. She has had no falls. The occupational therapy evaluation that was to be booked after the last visit was not arranged, and it is now booked for two weeks from today. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Medicine</td><td>Propranolol extended-release 60 mg daily; no side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Tremor</td><td>Hands steadier; head tremor unchanged</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None in six months</td></tr><tr><td>Occupational therapy</td><td>Not yet seen; booked for two weeks from today</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

