  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Essential tremor (G25.0)</content>. Stable benefit on propranolol, with TETRAS performance 15 and daily-living 8. Pulse 62 and no orthostatic drop. Occupational therapy is overdue. [S]<list><item>Continue propranolol extended-release 60 mg each morning.</item><item>Occupational therapy evaluation in two weeks.</item><item>Tremor review in about six months, and the yearly movement disorders review.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Voice tremor due to essential tremor (R49.8)</content>. Mild and well managed. [S]<list><item>Continue the voice strategies.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Tremor rating: TETRAS performance and activities of daily living subscales</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Performance subscale 15; daily-living subscale 8</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Archimedes spiral drawing and handwriting sample</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Small tremor waves; handwriting steady</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Examination for signs beyond tremor (rest tremor, bradykinesia, rigidity, dystonia, ataxia, cognitive change)</td><td>At diagnosis, then yearly or with a change in the tremor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No signs beyond tremor today; yearly neurology review due in the winter</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Resting heart rate and seated and 3-minute standing blood pressure</td><td>Every visit on a beta-blocker</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Pulse 62; 124/74 mmHg seated and 120/72 mmHg standing; the standing check missed at three months was done today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Beta-blocker safety: wheeze, slow pulse or heart block, fatigue, cold hands, low mood, hypoglycemia awareness</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No side effects</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Primidone safety: sedation, unsteadiness, nausea</td><td>Every visit on primidone</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not on primidone</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Drugs and substances that worsen tremor (beta-agonists, valproate, lithium, antidepressants, excess thyroid hormone, caffeine)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No new medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Fall query, with Timed Up and Go yearly</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No falls in six months; Timed Up and Go due at the wellness visit</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Mood (PHQ-9)</td><td>Before a beta-blocker, after starting it, then yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>PHQ-9 3 three months ago; mood good today</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>TSH and basic chemistry to exclude metabolic causes</td><td>Once at diagnosis; again only with a change in the tremor</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal at diagnosis</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Speech-language therapy for voice tremor</td><td>When voice tremor affects speech or work</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Course completed; strategies in use</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Occupational therapy for adaptive aids</td><td>When tremor limits daily tasks</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Recommended at the four-week visit but not booked for five months, a deviation from the plan. She managed by carrying cups half full and limiting writing, with no injury or loss of independence. Corrective action: the evaluation is booked for two weeks from today, and referrals are now tracked to completion</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Botulinum toxin for head or voice tremor</td><td>If head or voice tremor is disabling</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Head and voice tremor not disabling</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Referral for focused ultrasound thalamotomy or deep brain stimulation</td><td>If disabling limb tremor persists after adequate trials of propranolol and primidone</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Good response to propranolol; no disabling tremor</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Cognitive screen (MoCA)</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Up to date</td><td>MoCA 28 seven months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>AGS Beers Criteria medication review</td><td>Yearly from age 65</td><td>Up to date</td><td>No new medicines</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Advance care planning and goals of care</td><td>At least yearly from 65</td><td>Due</td><td>At the annual wellness visit in two months</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Vaccination status (influenza, pneumococcal, zoster, COVID-19, Tdap)</td><td>Yearly, per the CDC schedule</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza, pneumococcal, and zoster vaccines at the wellness visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Less hand tremor with daily tasks on a well-tolerated medicine, with resting heart rate 55 or above and no lightheadedness, by the three-month review. Outcome by 1980-05-05: TETRAS performance subscale fell from 22 to 16 and the activities of daily living subscale from 14 to 9 on propranolol; heart rate 64; no lightheadedness or falls [S]</item><item>Complete a course of voice therapy and use the strategies on stage. Outcome by 1980-05-05: Six-week course completed; steadier sustained notes with breath support and a slightly higher pitch [S]</item><item>Use adaptive aids for eating, drinking, and writing. In progress; target 1980-10-06 [S]</item><item>Name a health care agent and record her goals of care by the annual wellness visit. In progress; target 1980-10-06 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Evidence-based guideline update: treatment of essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2011); Practice parameter: therapies for essential tremor: report of the Quality Standards Subcommittee of the American Academy of Neurology (2005); Consensus Statement on the classification of tremors, from the task force on tremor of the International Parkinson and Movement Disorder Society (2018); MDS evidence-based review of treatments for essential tremor (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, general items for older adults (no essential tremor monograph) (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Occupational therapy in two weeks. Annual wellness visit in two months. Tremor review in about six months. Next scheduled visit 1980-10-06: subsequent annual wellness visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
